# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. One rule per line:
#   from   to   status
#
# Vercel reads vercel.json instead. GitHub Pages reads neither and will 404 on
# the old paths below, so if you host there, keep the old URLs alive some other
# way before you rename another page.

# B2B became Bulk Orders. Kept because "b2b" is a term agencies search for and
# may have been shared before the rename. 301 so any link equity follows.
/b2b        /bulk-orders/   301!
/b2b/*      /bulk-orders/   301!

# Common near-misses people type or that get shared with a stripped path.
/order/thankyou     /order/thank-you/   301
/visa-guides        /visa/              301
/visa-guide         /visa/              301
/faq.html           /faq/               301
/blog/index.html    /blog/              301

# Everything unmatched falls through to the real 404 with the right status.
# Without this some hosts serve a soft 404, which Google treats as a live page.
/*          /404.html       404
